# Ontology Layering and Semantic Promotion Boundary

## Why this contract exists

YAWN contains several true and useful loops. A recurring failure occurs when a
downstream mechanism is promoted into the root ontology or public mission merely
because it is vivid, newly articulated, or useful for one artifact.

The concrete regression that produced this contract was:

```text
Dave described graduation of agency as an internal flywheel.
A generated explainer promoted graduation of agency into the main story.
The artifact displaced coupling, relationship, and coordinated orientation.
```

The synthesis was fluent and internally coherent. It was still a category
error.

This contract adds an explicit layer system so future humans and agents can tell
what is foundational, what operates within the foundation, what governs action,
and what is merely a View or narrative projection.

## Canonical layer order

```text
L0  SUBSTRATE
    Reality, distinguishable Agents and Arenas, coupling, relationship,
    access, constraint, affordance, influence, and history.

L1  EPISTEMIC OPERATION
    Observation, trace, evidence, aperture, relevance, and orientation.

L2  ACTION / TRANSITION
    Intention, Projection, Move, Consequence, Proof, and Update.

L3  GOVERNANCE
    Authority, permission, delegation, autonomy, and graduation.

L4  PROJECTION / VIEW
    Interfaces, narratives, diagrams, slide decks, video, and other renderers.
```

The layers describe dependency and compilation order. They are not a claim that
reality is naturally partitioned into five boxes.

## Coupling and relationship

A **coupling** is a dependency or influence relation: changes in one pole alter,
constrain, enable, or become informative to another pole.

A **relationship** is the broader, history-dependent situated state through
which one or more couplings acquire access conditions, roles, stakes,
expectations, meanings, constraints, affordances, authority, and possible
movement.

```text
coupling = the dependency / influence skeleton
relationship = the inspectable situated state around that skeleton
```

Not every coupling is a full reflective relationship. Not every relationship
requires mutual psychological modeling. YAWN preserves the distinguishable
poles and does not turn Relationship into a mystical substance.

Relationship remains structurally prior to the operational loop because it
conditions what can become observable, relevant, possible, or authorized.
Observation remains operationally first because it is the first attributed
epistemic record an implementation can preserve.

## Agency and graduation

**Agency** is a cross-layer capacity. It is realized through an Agent's situated
access, model, values, action repertoire, authority, and feedback. It is not one
more substrate object and it is not automatically YAWN's terminal purpose.

**Graduation** is an L3 governance mechanism. Repeated proof may justify a
proposal to widen an agent's scope, trust, autonomy, or responsibility.
Graduation does not define the relationship, choose the human goal, or become
the public mission.

```text
graduation of agency
= optional internal proof-gated governance flywheel
≠ YAWN's ontology root
≠ YAWN's terminal objective
≠ a license to automate everything
```

## Public purpose boundary

The default public purpose is:

> Make consequential couplings and relationship states inspectable so distinct
> agents can establish shared reference, coordinate direction, take bounded
> action, and learn from consequences without losing authorship.

This permits orientation, agency, proof, and graduation to appear in the story,
but only in their proper roles.

The rightful human or collective retains authority over terminal goals,
meaning, consent, and consequential adoption. AI may help inspect, compare,
propose, simulate, and gather proof; it may not silently replace the direction
of the relationship.

## Narrative compilation rule

Every explainer, presentation, route, diagram, or video that claims to explain
YAWN as a whole MUST declare:

```yaml
root_subject:
  term:
  layer:
  statement:

public_purpose:

primary_loop: []

supporting_mechanisms:
  - term:
    layer:
    role:

internal_flywheel: []
terminal_goal_owner:
not_claimed: []
source_intent:
```

The root subject MUST compile from L0 unless the ontology contract itself has
been versioned through the semantic promotion gate.

A downstream term MAY be the subject of a specialized explainer. It MUST NOT be
presented as the purpose of the entire system merely because that explainer is
about it.

## Source-intent preservation

Explicit role language from the rightful author is authoritative for artifact
hierarchy unless it conflicts with an accepted constitutional contract.

Examples:

```text
"This is an internal flywheel."
→ supporting mechanism, not public mission

"This is one way to look at it."
→ View, not ontology replacement

"I think this may be the root; pressure-test it."
→ candidate constitutional proposal, not accepted root
```

Emphasis, excitement, repetition, rhetorical polish, visual prominence, or AI
fluency do not constitute semantic promotion.

## Semantic promotion gate

A term can move upward only through a visible, versioned change that includes:

1. an explicit RFC or constitutional proposal;
2. counterexamples and pressure tests;
3. evidence that the simpler ontology fails;
4. affected schema and migration analysis;
5. affected public language, interface, and action-policy analysis;
6. rightful maintainer adoption; and
7. a versioned contract update with rollback or supersession history.

No generated slide deck, video, summary, homepage, or code comment may perform
this promotion implicitly.

## Regression rule

The following compilation MUST fail:

```yaml
root_subject:
  term: graduation
  layer: governance
public_purpose: Graduate agents toward goals.
```

The corrected compilation is:

```yaml
root_subject:
  term: relationship
  layer: substrate
public_purpose: >
  Help distinct agents inspect their consequential couplings, establish shared
  reference, coordinate direction, act within authority, and learn.
supporting_mechanisms:
  - term: graduation
    layer: governance
    role: Widen bounded autonomy only after repeated proof.
```

## Stable shorthand

```text
Coupling first.
Relationship made inspectable.
Orientation made shareable.
Agency made accountable.
Graduation earned through proof.
Views remain Views.
```

## Agent Orientation Elevation

```yaml
agent_orientation:
  first_answer: "You are here"
  role: "visible inference, not hidden authority"
  current_state: "YAWN has rich concepts but previously lacked enforced layer ownership."
  possible_state: "Every artifact preserves substrate, operation, governance, and View boundaries."
  lacuna: "Whether the layer system remains sufficient under future counterexamples."
  movement: "Validate every whole-system explainer against the machine-readable layering contract."
  proof: "Regression tests reject orientation or graduation when promoted into the substrate root."
  boundary: "This contract guides compilation; it does not claim a final metaphysics."
```
